INT. MASCOT DRESSING ROOM, MINOR-LEAGUE BALLPARK - DAY

A cramped cinderblock closet crowded with giant heads: a hot dog, a gopher, a foam eagle with a bent beak. It smells of old sweat and glue.

ZEPHYR OKONJO, twenties, half-dressed as the gopher, struggles with a zipper. MORGANA TREVINO, fifties, the mascot coordinator, clutches a clipboard. DUNCAN, nineteen, the hot dog, stands frozen with one arm in a sleeve.

MORGANA
Showtime in four minutes!

ZEPHYR
My zipper's stuck!

DUNCAN
I can't see out of this thing!

MORGANA
You don't need to see, Duncan, you need to wave.

Zephyr yanks. Duncan staggers. Both of them knock into Morgana, who drops the clipboard. All three go down in a heap of foam and fur, the gopher head rolling away, the hot dog bun flapping.

ZEPHYR
Get off my tail!

DUNCAN
That's my mustard!

MORGANA
Both of you, stand up!

They stand, tangled. A voice booms through the wall.

ANNOUNCER (O.S.)
Ladies and gentlemen, please welcome your Oakwood Gophers!

The three look at each other. Zephyr picks up the gopher head, jams it on backwards, and runs for the door.
